### ClearWood Furnitures — Prompt 3 (Auth, RBAC, sessions, audit)
### VS Code REST Client (humao.rest-client). Start the API first: npm run dev:backend
### Run top to bottom — later requests reuse values captured from earlier ones.
###
### COOKIES: REST Client keeps its own cookie jar, so cw_adm_* / cw_cus_* are sent automatically.
### The refresh token is ONLY ever in the httpOnly cookie — it is never in a response body.
### Authenticated calls below use `Authorization: Bearer` because Bearer requests are CSRF-exempt;
### the production frontends use the cookies plus an X-CSRF-Token header instead.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:7180
@api = {{baseUrl}}/api/v1
@adminEmail = admin@clearwood.local
@adminPassword = ChangeMe@12345
# Step 1b changes the password. To run the file again from the top, restore the seed credentials
# first: npm run admin:reset-password --workspace backend
@adminNewPassword = Sheesham-Walnut-2031

### ---------------------------------------------------------------- ADMIN ---

### 1. Sign in as the seeded bootstrap ADMIN (sets cw_adm_at / cw_adm_rt / cw_adm_csrf).
###    An ordinary ADMIN - never SUPER_ADMIN - with mustChangePassword=true.
# @name adminLogin
POST {{api}}/admin/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{adminEmail}}",
  "password": "{{adminPassword}}"
}

###
@adminToken = {{adminLogin.response.body.$.data.tokens.accessToken}}

### 1a. ENFORCED -> 403 PASSWORD_CHANGE_REQUIRED on every admin route until the password changes.
###     Only /auth/me, /auth/change-password, /auth/logout, /auth/logout-all and /auth/sessions stay open.
GET {{api}}/admin/catalog/categories?depth=1
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### 1b. Change it. The same session keeps working; the new password must differ from the current
###     one and can never be the published placeholder (422 otherwise).
POST {{api}}/admin/auth/change-password
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "currentPassword": "{{adminPassword}}",
  "newPassword": "{{adminNewPassword}}"
}

### 2. Who am I — roles + the effective permission list (79 for ADMIN, 86 for SUPER_ADMIN)
GET {{api}}/admin/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### 3. GUARD CHAIN PROOF — authenticate(ADMIN) + requirePermission(catalog.category.read)
GET {{api}}/admin/catalog/categories?depth=1
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### 4. Anonymous -> 401 NOT_AUTHENTICATED
GET {{api}}/admin/catalog/categories

### 5. The permission registry, grouped for the UI. Needs system.role.read, which only SUPER_ADMIN
###    holds by default: the bootstrap ADMIN gets 403 FORBIDDEN here.
GET {{api}}/admin/permissions
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### 6. Roles and their permission counts (SUPER_ADMIN only, as above)
# @name roles
GET {{api}}/admin/roles
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

###
@roleId = {{roles.response.body.data.0.id}}

### 7. Active sessions for this admin
GET {{api}}/admin/auth/sessions
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### 8. Audit trail (system.audit.read)
GET {{api}}/admin/audit-logs?action=LOGIN&limit=5
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### ------------------------------------------------------- 403 / RBAC PROOF ---

### 9. Create a CATALOG_MANAGER (system.user.create). Re-running returns 409 — that is fine.
POST {{api}}/admin/users
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "catalog.manager@clearwood.local",
  "name": "Catalog Manager",
  "password": "Sheesham-Teak-2026",
  "roleCodes": ["CATALOG_MANAGER"]
}

### 9a. DENIED -> 403 ROLE_NOT_GRANTABLE. No amplification: an ADMIN can create accounts at or
###     below its own level, never a SUPER_ADMIN (nor grant one, nor change or disable one ->
###     403 ADMIN_USER_NOT_MANAGEABLE). Every refusal is audited as a CRITICAL PERMISSION_DENIED.
POST {{api}}/admin/users
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "would-be.super@clearwood.local",
  "name": "Would Be Super",
  "password": "Sheesham-Teak-2026",
  "roleCodes": ["SUPER_ADMIN"]
}

### 10. Sign in as that manager
# @name managerLogin
POST {{api}}/admin/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "catalog.manager@clearwood.local",
  "password": "Sheesham-Teak-2026"
}

###
@managerToken = {{managerLogin.response.body.$.data.tokens.accessToken}}

### 10a. A password chosen by another admin must be changed at first sign-in (mustChangePassword
###      is true above); until then every business route answers 403 PASSWORD_CHANGE_REQUIRED.
POST {{api}}/admin/auth/change-password
Authorization: Bearer {{managerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "currentPassword": "Sheesham-Teak-2026",
  "newPassword": "Sheesham-Teak-Manager-2027"
}

### 11. Allowed: the manager holds catalog.category.read (36 permissions in total)
GET {{api}}/admin/catalog/categories?depth=1
Authorization: Bearer {{managerToken}}

### 12. DENIED -> 403 FORBIDDEN + an audited PERMISSION_DENIED row (needs system.role.create)
POST {{api}}/admin/roles
Authorization: Bearer {{managerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "code": "SHOULD_NOT_EXIST",
  "name": "Should not exist",
  "permissions": []
}

### 13. The denial is in the trail
GET {{api}}/admin/audit-logs?action=PERMISSION_DENIED&limit=5
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### 13a. One role with its permission codes (system.role.read - SUPER_ADMIN by default; 404 if
###      unknown).
GET {{api}}/admin/roles/{{roleId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### 13b. Set another admin's password (system.user.update). Same rule as any account change: only
###      someone who holds everything the target holds, so a SUPER_ADMIN only by a SUPER_ADMIN
###      (else 403 ADMIN_USER_NOT_MANAGEABLE); never your own (use change-password). Ends every
###      session of the target, forces a change at next sign-in, audited CRITICAL PASSWORD_RESET.
# @name managers
GET {{api}}/admin/users?search=catalog.manager
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

###
@managerId = {{managers.response.body.data.0.id}}

POST {{api}}/admin/users/{{managerId}}/password
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "newPassword": "Sheesham-Teak-Reset-2027" }

### --------------------------------------------------------- ADMIN SESSION ---

### 14. Rotate using the httpOnly cookie (no body token needed, none is returned)
POST {{api}}/admin/auth/refresh
Content-Type: application/json

{}

### 15. Replaying an already-rotated cookie would return 401 TOKEN_REUSE and kill the family.
###     REST Client always sends the newest cookie, so reuse is exercised by the test suite
###     (backend/tests/auth-admin.test.ts -> "refuses a replayed cookie").

### 16. Identical response whether or not the address exists (no account enumeration)
POST {{api}}/admin/auth/forgot-password
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "{{adminEmail}}" }

###
POST {{api}}/admin/auth/forgot-password
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "definitely-not-a-user@clearwood.local" }

### 17. Wrong password -> the same message as an unknown account
POST {{api}}/admin/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "{{adminEmail}}", "password": "wrong-password-here" }

### 18. Sign out (Bearer is CSRF-exempt; the browser sends X-CSRF-Token instead)
POST {{api}}/admin/auth/logout
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### ------------------------------------------------------------- CUSTOMER ---

### 19. Request an OTP. `devCode` is returned only because NODE_ENV !== production.
# @name otpRequest
POST {{api}}/auth/otp/request
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "phone": "919820000777",
  "purpose": "LOGIN"
}

###
@otpCode = {{otpRequest.response.body.$.data.devCode}}

### 20. Verify it — signs in, or creates the account when the number is new
# @name otpVerify
POST {{api}}/auth/otp/verify
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "destination": "919820000777",
  "code": "{{otpCode}}",
  "purpose": "LOGIN",
  "name": "OTP Shopper"
}

###
@customerToken = {{otpVerify.response.body.$.data.tokens.accessToken}}

### 21. The signed-in customer
GET {{api}}/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}

### 22. REALM ISOLATION — an admin token is not valid on a storefront route (401 TOKEN_INVALID)
GET {{api}}/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### 23. …and a customer token is not valid on an admin route (401 TOKEN_INVALID)
GET {{api}}/admin/catalog/categories
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}

### 24. Password login for the seeded demo customer
# @name customerLogin
POST {{api}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "identifier": "aarav.mehta@example.com",
  "password": "CustomerDemo@2026"
}

### 25. Rotate the storefront session over its cookie
POST {{api}}/auth/refresh
Content-Type: application/json

{}

### 26. Update the profile (cookie-authenticated PATCH would need X-CSRF-Token; Bearer is exempt)
PATCH {{api}}/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "marketingOptIn": true }

### 27. A blocked customer cannot even request a code (403 ACCOUNT_DISABLED)
POST {{api}}/auth/otp/request
Content-Type: application/json

{ "phone": "919810000003", "purpose": "LOGIN" }

### 28. Resend before the cooldown -> 429 OTP_RESEND_TOO_SOON
POST {{api}}/auth/otp/request
Content-Type: application/json

{ "phone": "919820000777", "purpose": "LOGIN" }

### 29. Sign out
POST {{api}}/auth/logout
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}

### 30. The generated spec now carries every auth schema
GET {{baseUrl}}/openapi.json
Accept: application/json
